# Line-ending policy (2026-10-08, docs/174): STORE EVERY FILE BYTE-FOR-BYTE, no conversion.
# Was `* text=auto eol=lf` (map 1's policy: normalize to LF so Radiant's CRLF re-saves never
# churn). It broke fresh clones: ~389 working files are CRLF on disk (written by Windows tools)
# and many build gates pin sha256s / string-compare those exact bytes - gen_tod_amp63.js
# --check (every build, even -GscOnly), the staff, roster, altar, inducer, perk, Thunder Smash
# and sign manifests, the size-pass state. A clone checked them out as LF and the FIRST gate
# failed. `-text` also overrides Git for Windows' system core.autocrlf=true. Cost: a tool that
# flips a file's line endings now shows as a whole-file change - commit it as written.
* -text

# Binaries - never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.flac binary
*.ogg binary
*.exr binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary
*.tga binary
*.dds binary
*.psd binary
*.iwi binary
*.xmodel_bin binary
*.xanim_bin binary
*.cast binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.7z binary
*.rar binary

# Blender masters and the fan FBX sources ride Git LFS (docs/174, 2026-10-08): GitHub refuses any
# file over 100 MB (reference_two.blend is 128 MB) and every re-save of a master is a full copy.
# Free tier = 10 GiB storage + 10 GiB download / month; the 22 files were ~1.0 GB when added.
*.blend filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fbx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
